      "message": "I found the root cause of test failed.\n```\njava.lang.AssertionError: stopSoftAp Timeout\njava.lang.AssertionError: stopSoftAp Timeout\n\tat org.junit.Assert.fail(Assert.java:89)\n\tat android.net.cts.util.CtsTetheringUtils$StopSoftApCallback.waitForSoftApStopped(CtsTetheringUtils.java:493)\n\tat android.net.cts.util.CtsTetheringUtils.expectSoftApDisabled(CtsTetheringUtils.java:509)\n\tat android.tethering.test.TetheringManagerTest.testEnableTethering_carrierUnsupportByConfigChange_noTetheringActive(TetheringManagerTest.java:457)\n```\n\nThis is because mCtsTetheringUtils.expectSoftApDisabled(); is to detect that wifi ap is enable or disable. In CTS, if wifi is turn on, and it does not call mTM.stopTethering(TETHERING_WIFI);, wifimanager will send the callback of WifiManager#WIFI_AP_STATE_ENABLED, and this will cause  the CTS test filtered and keep waiting WIFI_AP_STATE_DISABLED. So that the test finally get timeout event.\n\n\n```\n        @Override\n        public void onStateChanged(int state, int failureReason) {\n            if (state \u003d\u003d WifiManager.WIFI_AP_STATE_DISABLED) mWaiting.open();\n        }\n```\n\nIf we want to get WIFI_AP_STATE_DISABLED from WifiManager, we need to call mTM.stopTethering(TETHERING_WIFI).",
